1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,952
Welcome to Boop.

2
00:00:00,952 --> 00:00:04,697
Grow your kittens into cats, then line up three cats to win.

3
00:00:04,697 --> 00:00:05,967
Here is how to play.

4
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:10,435
Start with an empty six by six bed and eight kittens each.

5
00:00:10,435 --> 00:00:12,881
Keep your eight adult cats in reserve.

6
00:00:12,881 --> 00:00:16,715
Take turns placing one available piece on any empty square.

7
00:00:16,715 --> 00:00:19,425
You never move an existing piece by hand.

8
00:00:20,125 --> 00:00:26,571
The piece you place pushes every neighboring piece it can boop one square directly away, including diagonally.

9
00:00:26,571 --> 00:00:28,404
Both colors move, even your own.

10
00:00:28,404 --> 00:00:30,592
Here, all eight neighbors spread out.

11
00:00:31,292 --> 00:00:35,554
A piece pushed off the edge goes back to its owner's pool, ready to play again.

12
00:00:35,554 --> 00:00:36,592
It is not captured.

13
00:00:37,292 --> 00:00:39,002
An occupied square blocks a push.

14
00:00:39,002 --> 00:00:42,849
These two pieces cannot be pushed into each other, whatever their colors.

15
00:00:42,849 --> 00:00:47,925
And there are no chain reactions: a booped piece moves once, without pushing its new neighbors.

16
00:00:48,625 --> 00:00:54,457
After the pushes finish, check for three of your pieces in a row: across, down, or diagonally.

17
00:00:54,457 --> 00:00:55,837
Three kittens graduate.

18
00:00:55,837 --> 00:00:58,345
Remove them from the bed and retire them.

19
00:00:58,345 --> 00:01:03,550
Take three cats from reserve and put them in your pool, not on those empty squares.

20
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:08,056
Now you can place either a kitten or a cat from your pool.

21
00:01:08,056 --> 00:01:09,792
Cats boop kittens and cats.

22
00:01:09,792 --> 00:01:11,395
Kittens cannot boop cats.

23
00:01:11,395 --> 00:01:14,800
But cats still cannot push into an occupied square.

24
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:17,238
A row can mix your kittens and cats.

25
00:01:17,238 --> 00:01:21,259
Remove all three; graduate the kittens, and return the existing cats to your pool.

26
00:01:21,259 --> 00:01:24,883
You always have eight active pieces, split between your pool and the bed.

27
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:31,062
If all eight of your pieces are on the bed, you may remove one kitten and graduate it into a cat in your pool.

28
00:01:31,062 --> 00:01:33,425
Or return an existing cat to your pool instead.

29
00:01:34,125 --> 00:01:38,227
If several rows qualify, or a longer line forms, choose one group of three.

30
00:01:38,227 --> 00:01:43,050
If you also have eight pieces out, choose the row or the single-piece option, not both.

31
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:48,552
Win with three of your adult cats in a row, across, down, or diagonally.

32
00:01:48,552 --> 00:01:51,595
Or win with all eight of your cats on the bed.

33
00:01:51,595 --> 00:01:54,300
Only check after every push is finished.

34
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,727
That is it: place, boop, then check for a win or graduation.

35
00:01:58,727 --> 00:02:02,960
Protect your pairs, watch the edges, and make a little room to grow.

36
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:03,592
Your turn.
